      "kind": "claim",
      "title": "The selector normal core completely classifies quotient-arithmetic behavior",
      "body": "A normal K is selector-admissible for c iff K subset Core_G(Stab_R(c)). Thus two selectors have identical admissible normal-kernel down-sets iff their normal cores agree. Since resonance labels depend only on G and K, this also classifies the entire decorated quotient-arithmetic lattice.",
      "entity_id": "claim:550c2ddd600514f26474"
    },
    {
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "test",
      "kind": "test",
      "title": "S3 unequal-stabilizer equal-core hostile separator",
      "body": "The fully labelled S3 selector and the coset selector for a nonnormal order-two subgroup have stabilizer orders 1 and 2 but both cores are trivial. Exact enumeration shows both admit only the trivial normal kernel.",
      "entity_id": "test:d44fc7a60b9323781555"
